SUMMARY:GitHub Copilot CLI Hands-On: Using MCP to Connect to External Syst
 ems
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nChapters Covered: 06 – Connect to
  GitHub\, Databases & APIs\n\n------------------------------------------\n
 \nIn this final session\, you'll learn how to use Model Context Protocol (
 MCP) servers to connect GitHub Copilot CLI to external systems so it can w
 ork with GitHub\, local files\, documentation\, databases\, APIs\, and mor
 e from the terminal. You'll learn why MCP matters\, how to add an MCP serv
 er\, and how GitHub Copilot CLI uses that functionality. The sessions will
  then wrap up with a course review so you leave with a clear picture of ho
 w the pieces fit together and how to apply them in your own projects.\n\nT
 his is the final session in the series that walks you through the [GitHub 
 Copilot CLI for Beginners course](https://github.com/github/copilot-cli-fo
 r-beginners).\n\nThis session is a part of a series. Learn more [here](htt
 ps://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1648/?wt.mc_id=meetup_S-1648
 _webpage_reactor)\n\nPre-requisites:\nComplete [**Chapter 00**](https://gi
 thub.com/github/copilot-cli-for-beginners/blob/main/00-quick-start/README.
 md) and have GitHub Copilot CLI installed and signed in\n\n---------------
 --------------------------------------------------------\n\n[⏱🌎 This 
 series is offered in two time zones for your convenience. Looking for our 
 APAC sessions? Click here.](https://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series
 /S-1651/?wt.mc_id=1reg_26905_webpage_reactor)
